course: dictionary
lesson: 15462
title: Stirred: mixing, moving and feeling
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Stir, stirs, stirred and stirring all come from one verb, so they share a main idea: moving something round or making it move. «She stirred the soup with a wooden spoon.» The spoon is the clue. Stirred means mixed by moving something round and round.
explain: Read the words around stirred to find its meaning. «The baby stirred in her cot.» Nobody is mixing anything here, so stirred must mean moved a little, as if starting to wake up.
explain: Stirred can also describe feelings. «The old song stirred memories of her grandma.» The song did not move anything you can see. It made her feel something strong. To check, swap in a meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Stir, stirs, stirred and stirring are all forms of the same verb.
fact: «Stirred» can mean mixed by moving a spoon round and round, as in «stirred the sugar into the tea».
fact: «Stirred» can mean moved a little, especially after being still or asleep.
fact: «Stirred» can mean made someone feel a strong feeling, such as sadness or excitement.
fact: «Stirred up» means caused trouble or strong feelings.
exercise: «She stirred the sugar into her tea.» What does stirred mean here? | *Mixed by moving a spoon round and round | Stopped and sat still | Dropped on the floor
exercise: «The cat stirred on the warm mat, then went back to sleep.» What does stirred mean here? | Ran away from the mat | *Moved a little, as if starting to wake | Painted the mat bright red
exercise: «The news stirred up a lot of anger in the town.» What does stirred up mean? | Made the town smaller | Told a joke | Cleaned the streets | *Caused trouble or strong feelings
test: «The music stirred her heart, and she began to cry happily.» What does stirred mean here? | Mixed it with water | Dropped her bag | Turned the music off | *Made her feel a strong feeling
test: «He stirred up the other children with a lie.» What does stirred up mean? | Fell asleep | *Caused trouble | Tidied the classroom | Fed the ducks
exam: Which sentence uses stirred to mean mixed by moving a spoon? | «The film stirred her deeply.» | «The crowd stirred up trouble.» | *«Mum stirred the custard until it was smooth.» | «The dog stirred from its sleep.»
